{%- liquid
  assign is_instrument = false
  assign has_tshirt = false
  assign ship_date = blank
  for t in product.tags
    if t == 'instrument'
      assign is_instrument = true
    endif
    if t == 'free-tshirt'
      assign has_tshirt = true
    endif
    if t contains 'ships:'
      assign ship_date = t | remove: 'ships:'
    endif
  endfor
  comment
    ships: is a permanent date source, not a state switch — only a FUTURE
    date means pre-order; a passed date means the batch has landed.
  endcomment
  assign ship_future = false
  if ship_date != blank
    assign now_s = 'now' | date: '%s' | plus: 0
    assign ship_s = ship_date | date: '%s' | plus: 0
    if ship_s > now_s
      assign ship_future = true
    endif
  endif
  assign variant = product.selected_or_first_available_variant | default: product.variants.first
  assign cases = collections['cases'].products
  assign sl_name = product.title | remove: ' - 440Hz' | remove: '- 440Hz' | remove: ' - Ember Steel' | escape
-%}

{%- comment -%} Phase 0 shortlist heart, used twice: over the gallery photo and
    beside Add to cart. Icon-only both times — a text row under the price cost
    ~70px of column height, which pushed the videos and scale switcher down. {%- endcomment -%}
{%- capture shortlist_heart_svg -%}
<svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="17" height="17" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M12 20.3C7.2 16.6 3.5 13.5 3.5 9.9 3.5 7.2 5.6 5 8.2 5c1.5 0 3 .7 3.8 1.9C12.8 5.7 14.3 5 15.8 5c2.6 0 4.7 2.2 4.7 4.9 0 3.6-3.7 6.7-8.5 10.4z" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg>
{%- endcapture -%}

<section
  class="section product-section full-width"
  data-handle="{{ product.handle }}"
  data-variant="{{ variant.id }}"
  data-price="{{ product.price | money }}"
  data-cents="{{ product.price }}"
  data-compare="{% if product.compare_at_price > product.price %}{{ product.compare_at_price | money }}{% endif %}"
  data-available="{{ product.available }}"
>
  {%- comment -%}
    No visual breadcrumb: the fixed header keeps the range one click away and
    the whole range sits at the foot of the page. The hierarchy lives in
    BreadcrumbList JSON-LD (snippets/meta-tags.liquid) instead, which is what
    search results actually read.
  {%- endcomment -%}
  {%- comment -%}
    Four grid children, placed by named areas (see .product-grid). The head is
    its own block rather than living inside .product-info so mobile can lift
    the name and price above the photo — you cannot reorder across parents.
  {%- endcomment -%}
  <div class="product-grid">
    <div class="product-head">
      <h1>{{ product.title | remove: ' - 440Hz' | remove: '- 440Hz' | replace: 'Ember Steel', 'Ember Steel®' }}</h1>
      <div class="product-meta">
        {% render 'availability-badge', product: product %}
        <p class="product-price">
          {%- if product.compare_at_price > product.price -%}
            <s>{{ product.compare_at_price | money }}</s>
          {%- endif -%}
          {{ product.price | money }}
        </p>
        {%- comment -%} TEMP A/B — remove before the public domain launch
            (see docs and the go-live checklist). Desktop only, wired in
            ayasa.js; version B = big carousel above Keep exploring +
            Order-now buy flow. {%- endcomment -%}
        <button type="button" class="pdp-ab" id="pdpAb" hidden>
          <span class="pdp-ab-dot" aria-hidden="true"></span><span id="pdpAbLabel">Layout A</span>
        </button>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="product-gallery">
      <div class="product-photo" id="productPhoto">
        {%- if product.featured_image -%}
          {{ product.featured_image | image_url: width: 1200 | image_tag: widths: '600, 900, 1200', alt: product.featured_image.alt | default: product.title }}
        {%- endif -%}
        <button type="button" class="gal-nav gal-prev" id="galPrev" hidden aria-label="Previous image">‹</button>
        <button type="button" class="gal-nav gal-next" id="galNext" hidden aria-label="Next image">›</button>
        {%- if is_instrument -%}
          <button type="button" class="shortlist-heart" data-handle="{{ product.handle }}" data-name="{{ sl_name }}"
            aria-label="Add {{ sl_name }} to shortlist" title="Add to shortlist" aria-pressed="false">{{ shortlist_heart_svg }}</button>
        {%- endif -%}
      </div>
      <div class="product-thumbs" id="productThumbs">
        {%- for image in product.images -%}
          <button type="button" class="product-thumb{% if forloop.first %} active{% endif %}" data-src="{{ image | image_url: width: 1200 }}" aria-label="Photo {{ forloop.index }}">
            {{ image | image_url: width: 160, height: 160, crop: 'center' | image_tag: loading: 'lazy', alt: '' }}
          </button>
        {%- endfor -%}
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="product-info">
      <div class="product-notes" id="productNotes" hidden>
        <div class="notemap">
          <span id="productNoteMap"></span>
          <p class="notemap-bottom" id="productNoteBottom"></p>
        </div>
      </div>

      {%- comment -%} clamped to two lines on mobile; the button is revealed by
          ayasa.js only when the text actually overflows {%- endcomment -%}
      <div class="product-desc" id="productDesc">{{ product.description }}</div>
      <button type="button" class="desc-more" id="descMore" hidden>Read more</button>

      <form id="buyForm" action="{{ routes.cart_add_url }}" method="post">
        <input type="hidden" name="id" value="{{ variant.id }}">
        <input type="hidden" name="quantity" value="1">

        {%- comment -%} on mobile the choices stay folded behind an "Order now"
            step (wired in ayasa.js); desktop shows them as before {%- endcomment -%}
        <div class="buy-options" id="buyOptions"><div class="buy-options-inner">
        {%- if is_instrument -%}
          <div class="product-option">
            <label for="caseSelect">Handpan case <span class="option-required">required — we pack every instrument in a proper case so it arrives safely</span></label>
            {%- comment -%} the select stays as the (hidden) source of truth for all cart logic;
                the visual picker below drives it {%- endcomment -%}
            {%- comment -%} no `required` attr: the select is hidden and a hidden required field
                blocks native form submission before the JS validation can run {%- endcomment -%}
            <select id="caseSelect">
              <option value="" selected disabled>Please choose a case…</option>
              {%- for c in cases -%}
                {%- assign cv = c.selected_or_first_available_variant | default: c.variants.first -%}
                <option value="{{ cv.id }}" data-price="{{ c.price }}" {% unless c.available %}disabled{% endunless %}>
                  {{ c.title }} — {{ c.price | money }}{% unless c.available %} (out of stock){% endunless %}
                </option>
              {%- endfor -%}
            </select>
            <button type="button" class="case-trigger" id="caseTrigger" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="casePickerWrap">
              <span class="case-trigger-label">Please choose a case…</span>
              <span class="case-trigger-chev" aria-hidden="true">▾</span>
            </button>
            <div class="case-picker-wrap" id="casePickerWrap">
              <div class="case-picker" id="casePicker">
                {%- for c in cases -%}
                  {%- assign cv = c.selected_or_first_available_variant | default: c.variants.first -%}
                  <button type="button" class="case-card" data-variant="{{ cv.id }}" {% unless c.available %}disabled{% endunless %} aria-pressed="false">
                    <span class="case-thumb">
                      {%- if c.featured_image -%}
                        {{ c.featured_image | image_url: width: 200 | image_tag: loading: 'lazy', alt: c.title }}
                      {%- endif -%}
                    </span>
                    <span class="case-name">{{ c.title | remove: 'Evatek 2.0 ' }}</span>
                    <span class="case-price">{{ c.price | money }}{% unless c.available %} · out of stock{% endunless %}</span>
                  </button>
                {%- endfor -%}
              </div>
            </div>
            {%- if cases.size == 0 -%}
              <p class="option-note">⚠ The “Cases” collection is empty — create it per import/IMPORT-GUIDE.md.</p>
            {%- endif -%}
          </div>
        {%- endif -%}

        {%- if has_tshirt -%}
          <div class="product-option" id="shirtOption">
            <label for="shirtSize">Free Ayasa t-shirt</label>
            {%- comment -%} the selects stay as the source of truth for the cart
                (and for the lightbox buy bar); the visual picker drives them {%- endcomment -%}
            <div class="option-row" hidden>
              <select id="shirtSize" name="properties[Free t-shirt size]">
                <option value="" selected disabled>Please choose a t-shirt…</option>
                <option value="No free t-shirt">No free t-shirt</option>
                <option>EU Small / US Extra Small</option>
                <option>EU Medium / US Small</option>
                <option>EU Large / US Medium</option>
                <option>EU XL / US Large</option>
                <option>EU XXL / US XL</option>
                <option>EU XXXL / US XXL</option>
              </select>
              <select id="shirtColor" name="properties[Free t-shirt color]" aria-label="T-shirt color">
                <option>Black</option>
                <option>Off-white</option>
                <option>Khaki</option>
              </select>
            </div>

            {%- comment -%} same trigger + drop-down pattern as the case picker {%- endcomment -%}
            <button type="button" class="case-trigger" id="shirtTrigger" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="shirtPickerWrap">
              <span class="case-trigger-label" id="shirtTriggerLabel">Please choose a t-shirt…</span>
              <span class="case-trigger-chev" aria-hidden="true">▾</span>
            </button>
            {%- comment -%} TEMP: case product photos stand in until the three
                t-shirt shots land (then swap to tshirt-black/-offwhite/-khaki) {%- endcomment -%}
            <div class="case-picker-wrap" id="shirtPickerWrap">
            <div class="shirt-picker" id="shirtPicker">
              {%- assign shirt_colors = 'Black,Off-white,Khaki' | split: ',' -%}
              {%- for color in shirt_colors -%}
                {%- assign placeholder = cases[forloop.index0] -%}
                <button type="button" class="shirt-card" data-color="{{ color }}" aria-pressed="false">
                  <span class="shirt-thumb">
                    {%- if placeholder.featured_image -%}
                      {{ placeholder.featured_image | image_url: width: 400 | image_tag: loading: 'lazy', alt: color }}
                    {%- endif -%}
                  </span>
                  <span class="shirt-name">{{ color }}</span>
                </button>
              {%- endfor -%}
              <button type="button" class="shirt-card shirt-none" data-color="" aria-pressed="false">
                <span class="shirt-none-text">No t-shirt,<br>thanks</span>
              </button>
            </div>
            </div>

            {%- comment -%} chips are built by ayasa.js from the select's own
                options, so the sizes live in exactly one place {%- endcomment -%}
            <div class="shirt-sizes" id="shirtSizes" hidden>
              <p class="shirt-sizes-label">Your size</p>
              <div class="size-chips" id="sizeChips"></div>
            </div>
          </div>
        {%- endif -%}
        </div></div>

        <p class="option-error" id="buyError" hidden></p>

        {%- comment -%} live total (handpan + chosen case) — appears once a case
            is picked; on mobile also during the Order-now step as "+ case" {%- endcomment -%}
        <p class="buy-total" id="buyTotal" hidden></p>

        <div class="buy-row">
          {%- if product.available -%}
            <button type="submit" class="btn btn-primary product-buy">
              {%- if ship_future -%}Pre-order. Ships {{ ship_date | date: '%-d %B %Y' }}{%- else -%}Add to cart{%- endif -%}
            </button>
          {%- else -%}
            <button type="button" class="btn btn-ghost product-buy" disabled>Sold out</button>
          {%- endif -%}
          {%- if is_instrument -%}
            <button type="button" class="shortlist-btn shortlist-btn-icon" data-handle="{{ product.handle }}" data-name="{{ sl_name }}"
              aria-label="Add {{ sl_name }} to shortlist" title="Add to shortlist" aria-pressed="false">{{ shortlist_heart_svg }}</button>
          {%- endif -%}
        </div>
      </form>
    </div>

    {% comment %}
      "The sound" — performance videos, rendered by ayasa.js from the model
      data (ayasa-data.js) when this product has demo clips. A grid child, not
      a gallery child: on desktop it fills the dead space under the thumbnails
      beside the buy area; on mobile the column stacks it below the buy button.
    {% endcomment %}
    <div class="product-demos" id="productDemos" hidden>
      <div class="demo-strip" id="demoStrip"></div>
    </div>
  </div>

  {%- if is_instrument -%}
    {% comment %}
      Keep exploring — the whole range, always open, rendered by ayasa.js.
      Filter pills top and bottom (one shared state) so a long grid can be
      re-filtered without scrolling back up.
    {% endcomment %}
    <div class="keep-exploring" id="scaleNav" data-current="{{ product.handle }}">
      <div class="section-head reveal">
        <p class="kicker">Keep exploring</p>
      </div>
      {%- comment -%} second pill row is injected mid-body, between the cards and
          "Find something special" — see initScaleNav {%- endcomment -%}
      <div class="scale-filters" role="group" aria-label="Filter scales"></div>
      <div class="scale-panel-body"></div>
    </div>
  {%- endif -%}
</section>

{% schema %}
{
  "name": "Ayasa product",
  "settings": [],
  "disabled_on": { "groups": ["header", "footer"] }
}
{% endschema %}
